From ea2b9999c8cf037f5d96afc011ec311a0bd514d1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ravindra Lakkireddy <85186928+rlakki08@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 03:53:36 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 06/11] feat: sizes printed in the listing title as the
 last-resort dims source

Integration finding #15 follow-up: a candidate the LLM, Home Depot and the page fetch can't size
is dropped even when its title prints the size. sellers.parse_title_sizes reads the one size
mention in a title -- "3 in. (76 mm)" (the printed metric wins), "3-3/4 in.", "1-1/4in.",
"12 in. x 8 in.", "10 in. x12 in.", "12 x 8 inch", "36 in. W x 24 in. D x 34.5 in. H" -- and is
conservative: a number needs a length unit; alternatives ("3 or 3-3/4 in. (76/96 mm)"), screw
gauges ("#8 x 1-1/4 in."), centre-to-centre / hole-centre spacing, radii, overlays and cups are
never sizes; two separate size mentions in one title mean "don't know".

search._dims_from_title runs only after the page fallback and only completes a box, never guesses
a side: W/D/H-labelled sizes take their axis, three unlabelled ones follow _parse_dims' flat-goods
rule (thinnest = depth, longest = height), and one unlabelled size may only fill the single side
the LLM's published dims left empty. dims_source "title" (documented in api.md).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
